    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d237-a6">

                <pb facs="0439" n="339" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg339"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 6 in No. 87.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Knott to the
                            President.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >State of Kentucky, Executive Department</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Frankfort</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1884-07-03"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi>
                            3, 1884</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to hand you the inclosed
                    communication from Hon. Samuel B. Berry, of Lebanon, Ky., requesting your
                    excellency to use your good offices in obtaining from the Italian Government
                    leave for Rev. Father Valentine Theodore Lanciotti, vice-president of St. Mary’s
                    College, to visit his aged parents at Ciciliano, Italy, to which I beg leave to
                    add my hearty indorsement.</p>
                <p>I know Father Lanciotti intimately, and can commend him as a most excellent and
                    exemplary gentleman, if, indeed, his position as second officer of one of the
                    oldest and most distinguished institutions of learning in the valley of the
                    Mississippi were not sufficient without it. I would be extremely gratified
                    personally, as I am confident the very large circle of friends and patrons of
                    the college as well as of Father Lanciotti would be, if the permission be asks
                    could be obtained; and I trust I am not tresspassing either upon your time or
                    your generous disposition in asking this favor for an esteemed neighbor and
                    friend.</p>
                <p>With sentiments, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. PROCTOR KNOTT.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
